From 78498c040ee424fd0376a219b572bda7e6e1279b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 04:00:58 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(rest): sign a cached path in the lattice form the file
 stores

path_sig hashed every move float bit-exact, while the project file
writes moves through the 1 um lattice snap. A generated path off the
lattice (threading's y = 6.050000000000001) then signed differently
after save and load (6.05), so a dependent op's rest digest no longer
matched and the second op of a chain reopened Stale. Hash each float
snapped to the lattice instead: on-lattice paths sign exactly as
before, a change of half a micron or more still moves the signature.

Pinned by turning_thread::a_chain_of_threading_ops_stays_ok_through_save_and_load.

Fixes #1351

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
